  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7d081f29-e5f0-532b-a135-8601fed6cef4" activityNameId="61998323-c6f7-5783-bb62-6f327d431144" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Horn meal, at regional storehouse</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Horn meal, at regional storehouse
Values regarding energy requirements were approximated from the energy consumption, which is typical for bone meal production in the European Union.;
UUID: fb3b4b81-6dc6-3385-8dca-9c8df7b0e187
Energy demand required for sterilisation of horns by autoclave and subsequent milling to horn meal were taken into account. Transports from a manufacturer in India, representing the most important country of production of horn meal for the Swiss market, to the regional storehouse in Switzerland were supplemented. No process emissions were taken into account. Infrastructure and land use were included by means of proxy data.
Location: The values refer to the market situation in Switzerland. 
Technology: Values refer to a commonly used technology for this product.
Time period: Year of publication of the reference from which the energy demand of further processing was taken from. 
Production volume: 2300 tons used in Switzerland in 1998.
Sampling: Data approximate production of horn meal in India, from where the largest part of horn meal consumption in Switzerland is imported. 
Extrapolations: Energy requirements for further processing of horns to horn meal in India approximated from the situation in Europe.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fb3b4b81-6dc6-3385-8dca-9c8df7b0e187.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
